The attached image compares local inflammation in mouse muscle tissue two weeks after injection of aluminum hydroxide adjuvant (AH) (left) versus Nano-11 (right) with an antigen. The left panel, representing AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation (asterisk) with dense aggregates of macrophages and eosinophils around skeletal muscle (M). The right panel, representing Nano-11, reveals much less residual inflammation (asterisk) and fewer macrophages, indicating that Nano-11 induces a more transient and less severe inflammatory response compared to AH.